/*
====================================================================
In this scenario, the system is initialized in dynamics mode
at hour 10 of a typical clear day irradiance profile. The system
is initialized, and the PV delivers power to the grid. Then,
100 ms later, a three-phase line-to-ground fault occurs at Bus
3 and remains for 100 ms before being cleared. The effects
in voltage and the current delivered by the PV system during
these interactions are stored in the PV* monitors.
====================================================================

Davis Montenegro and Robert Kerestes

2024

*/


! Comment out the line below if running from OpenDSS-G 
!Compile master.dss

! Forces the PV to deliver power during the fault event 
pvsystem.pv1.safevoltage=0.5

solve

set mode=dynamics maxiterations=50 number=100 time=(10,0)
solve

New Fault.myFault phases=3 bus1=n3
solve

Fault.myFault.enabled=Falses
solve


! Use the plot routines below to plot the monitors using DSSView from stand alone DSS 
/*

! Export monitors
export monitors all

! active power output
plot monitor object=myPVPQ channels=(1,3, 5)
! Voltages at the PV Point of connection
plot monitor object=myPVVolt channels=(1,3, 5)
! Currents at the PV Point of connection
plot monitor object=myPVVolt channels=(7,9, 11)
*/